          {
            "abbreviated": false,
            "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Jaeger's 4-flow theorem: every finite 4-edge-connected simple graph has a nowhere-zero integer 4-flow, i.e. an antisymmetric function on darts with values in {\u00b11, \u00b12, \u00b13} that is conserved at every vertex. Also proved: a graph with two edge-disjoint spanning trees has its edges covered by two even subgraphs (a nowhere-zero \u2124\u2082 \u00d7 \u2124\u2082-flow) and has a nowhere-zero integer 4-flow. Version 2 adds Jaeger's 8-flow theorem: every finite bridgeless graph has its edges covered by three even subgraphs and has a nowhere-zero integer 8-flow; conversely a graph with a nowhere-zero flow has no bridge. Version 3 adds Seymour's 6-flow theorem (every finite bridgeless graph has a nowhere-zero integer 6-flow) and Tutte's theorem relating group and integer flows (for k > 0, every nowhere-zero \u2124/k-flow \u03c6 lifts to a nowhere-zero integer k-flow \u03c8 with \u03c8 \u2261 \u03c6 mod k, and conversely an integer k-flow reduces modulo k to a nowhere-zero \u2124/k-flow). Mathlib has no flows.",
            "authors": [
              {
                "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
              }
            ],
            "classification": {
              "arxiv": [
                "math.CO"
              ],
              "msc2020": [
                "05C21",
                "05C40"
              ]
            },
            "formalization": {
              "theorem_names": [
                "JaegerFlow.exists_even_cover_of_trees",
                "JaegerFlow.exists_flow_of_trees",
                "JaegerFlow.jaeger_four_flow",
                "EightFlowTheorem.exists_even_cover_three",
                "EightFlowTheorem.jaeger_eight_flow",
                "EightFlowTheorem.not_isBridge_of_flow",
                "SixFlowTheorem.integer_flow_of_zmod",
                "SixFlowTheorem.zmod_flow_of_integer",
                "SixFlowTheorem.seymour_six_flow"
              ]
            },
